<%--
Spreadsheet_Viewer

Displays a workbook AS A GRID - the cells, their fonts, fills and borders - rather than as a
paginated print-out. Registered for the spreadsheet mimes in config('rsx.preview.viewers').

WHY NOT Pdf_Viewer, WHICH SERVED THESE BEFORE. A spreadsheet has no pages. Asked for a PDF,
LibreOffice applies its PRINT model: page breaks through the middle of the data, the print area
only, and by default neither gridlines nor row and column headers. The result is faithful to a
print-out nobody asked for and unrecognisable as the grid it is previewing. Exporting an image
instead changes nothing - the print model survives the output format, because the format was
never the problem.

The rendition is HTML produced by PhpSpreadsheet (Spreadsheet_Rendition) and served by
File_Preview_Controller::sheet_rendition. Formulas are never evaluated: a workbook stores the
cached RESULT of every formula, which is what the author last saw, and that is what shows.

IT IS AN IFRAME, AND SANDBOXED, FOR TWO SEPARATE REASONS.

  SECURITY. Cell values are other people's input rendered into markup. The rendition is purified
  when it is generated and the response carries its own restrictive CSP, and this is the third
  layer: `sandbox` with neither allow-scripts nor allow-same-origin means that even markup that
  somehow survived both cannot execute and cannot reach this origin.

  STYLE ISOLATION, which matters more often. The rendition carries the WORKBOOK's fonts, sizes
  and borders as inline styles. Rendered inline it would sit inside the application's own
  cascade - the theme's table rules, its border-collapse, its font stack - and the preview would
  show the workbook wearing this application's clothes. An iframe is a clean sheet, so what the
  reader sees is the document.

States, in the order the template tests them:
  render_status 'failed'   terminal - the workbook could not be read     -> (Preview Unavailable)
  rendition_url set        the rendition exists                          -> the grid
  otherwise                queued, or evicted from the LRU cache         -> (Preparing Preview...)

The waiting state is not a spinner that spins forever: this viewer subscribes to its attachment
in on_create(), and the frame the render worker publishes when the rendition lands swaps the grid
in with no reload and no polling. A rendition evicted by the LRU cleanup re-queues itself on the
first request for it (sheet_rendition), so this state is also the recovery path.

Args (the viewer contract Document_Preview passes to every dynamic viewer):
  $attachment_id (required) - the File_Attachment_Model id to read. Throws if absent.
  $file_name     (optional) - used as the iframe title, for assistive technology.

Events OUT: 'preview_loaded' {pages:1}. The grid scrolls; it does not paginate, so set_page is a
no-op and the host's page chrome stays hidden.
--%>
<Define:Spreadsheet_Viewer tag="div">
    <% if (!this.args.attachment_id) { throw new Error('Spreadsheet_Viewer requires $attachment_id'); } %>
    <%
        const _info = this.data.info;
        const _failed = this.data.error_data
            || (_info && _info.render_status_id === File_Storage_Model.RENDER_STATUS_FAILED);
        const _url = _info ? _info.urls.rendition : null;
    %>
    <div class="Spreadsheet_Viewer__frame">
        <% if (_failed) { %>
            <%-- Terminal. FAILED is never retried by the worker, so this is an end state and
                 says so plainly rather than implying something is still coming. --%>
            <div class="Spreadsheet_Viewer__notice">(Preview Unavailable)</div>
        <% } else if (!_url) { %>
            <%-- Queued, still rendering, or evicted from the rendition cache. The realtime
                 subscription in on_create brings us back the moment it exists. --%>
            <div class="Spreadsheet_Viewer__notice">(Preparing Preview...)</div>
        <% } else { %>
            <iframe class="Spreadsheet_Viewer__sheet"
                    src="<%= _url %>"
                    sandbox=""
                    title="<%= this.args.file_name || 'Spreadsheet preview' %>"></iframe>
        <% } %>
    </div>
</Define:Spreadsheet_Viewer>
